a67c77bc520a574c3f3007c45d9976909e8efdde142469daec35558c5","download_count":611,"created_at":"2026-09-28T00:22:50Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T00:22:51Z"}],"body":"<!-- cliproxyapi-linux-release-assets:start -->\n## Linux release assets\n\n- `CLIProxyAPI_<version>_linux_<arch>.tar.gz` is the default Linux build. It supports dynamic library plugins and is built against a GLIBC 2.17 baseline.\n- `CLIProxyAPI_<version>_linux_<arch>_no-plugin.tar.gz` is the portable Linux build for musl-based or older systems such as OpenWrt. It does not support dynamic library plugins.\n\n## FreeBSD release assets\n\n- `CLIProxyAPI_<version>_freebsd_aarch64_no-plugin.tar.gz` is the FreeBSD arm64 build. It is built without CGO and does not support dynamic library plugins.\n\n<!-- cliproxyapi-linux-release-assets:end -->\n\n## Changelog\n\n- fix(pluginhost): preserve disabled state in host auth callbacks (5756d76e)\n- feat(config): warn on unrecognized sections during v8 migration (01274e22)\n- fix(meta): strip unsupported search_content_types from web search tools (2c27e61f)\n- feat(openai): support quality parameter for xAI image requests (4b99d1d6)\n- fix(openai): prevent false positive namespace prefix matches in responses tools (4ad5bba7)\n- fix(translator): append trailing newlines to SSEEventData frames (0a45f253)\n- fix(gemini): preserve thought signatures in interactions translation (04f88169)\n- fix(discovery): support bonded interfaces and deduplicate build warnings (acdace93)\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/compare/v8.0.2...v8.0.3\n","reactions":{"total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0}}
